===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnˈhɛɹətəns/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-inheritance.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Recorded since 1473, {{suffix|inherit|ance|lang=en}}. More at {{m|en|inherit}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The passing of [[title]] to an [[estate]] upon death.
# {{lb|en|countable}} That which a person is entitled to [[inherit]], by law or [[testament]].
# {{lb|en|biology}} The biological [[attribute]]s passed [[hereditarily]] from ancestors to their [[offspring]].
# {{lb|en|programming|object-oriented}} In object-oriented programming, the mechanism whereby parts of a [[superclass]] are available to instances of its [[subclass]].

